  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="16">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 16</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-d">And freolsa ⁊ fæstena be wite healde man rihtlice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="16" corresp="#wit-d">And freolsa ⁊ fæstena be wite healde man rihtlice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And freolsa and fæstena be wite healde man rihtlice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And festivals and fasts shall be duly observed, under pain of incurring the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And feasts and fasts are to be properly observed or there will be a penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Feiertage und Fasten sollen bei Strafe gesetzmässig gehalten werden.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let feasts and fasts be kept rightly, on pain of a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="265"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_22">VI Atr 22</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 22</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 22.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
